After the shared recovery-chemistry Record, follow a recovered solvent, acid/base, salt or catalyst-related stream toward an actual user. Identify source variability, collected state, contaminants, recovery selectivity, product specification and evidence that the delivered material remains suitable over time.

Construct a closed constituent account with virgin input, use, collection, recovery, purges/losses and replacement. If a simple repeated loop recovers a fixed fraction r of an unchanged quantity each pass, the remaining fraction after n passes is rⁿ under those explicit assumptions. A real process may accumulate impurities or change function, so that arithmetic alone does not establish an indefinitely closed loop.

Compare internal reuse, shared external recovery and a virgin source on quality, logistics, utilities, analysis and continuity. Determine who owns residuals and supplies the necessary information. A recovery business may depend on a consistent feed quality or minimum volume; an interruption can affect both waste handling and incoming reagent availability. Develop a qualification/change study using full methods, uncertainty and alternatives. Connect the resulting physical/evidential history through ordinary Records and source references, preserving unresolved process or trade-secret gaps explicitly.

